<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-6001] [Metadata] Kylin4 metadata cannot be directly upgraded to Kylin5. After customers migrate the metadata, they still need to rebuild models and other components.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-6001</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Current method for upgrading from Kylin4 to Kylin5: &#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Back up the Kylin4 metadata, migrate it to Kylin5 using the data migration script, and then restore the migrated data. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Issue:&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
After restoring the Kylin5 data, the models need to be rebuilt before they can be used.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13608859">KYLIN-6001</key>
            <summary>[Metadata] Kylin4 metadata cannot be directly upgraded to Kylin5. After customers migrate the metadata, they still need to rebuild models and other components.</summary>
